{#- One author's portrait, at whichever size the caller needs.

    A macro rather than a plain include: Nunjucks includes share the caller's
    context, so parameters would have to be {% set %} beforehand and would
    leak afterwards. A macro takes them properly.

    The `avatar` filter returns a path when a portrait exists for that name
    and null when it does not, so the fallback figure lives here once instead
    of in every template that shows a person. Named `portrait` so it does not
    read as a collision with that filter.

    `alt` is empty in the list, where the name sits in the row beside it, and
    set on a thread, where this is the only place the sender appears. -#}
{% macro portrait(who, klass, size, lazy=false, alt="") -%}
{%- set face = who | avatar -%}
{%- if face -%}
<img class="{{ klass }}" alt="{{ alt }}" src="{{ face }}" width="{{ size }}" height="{{ size }}"{% if lazy %} loading="lazy"{% endif %}>
{%- else -%}
<svg class="{{ klass }} avatar-other" viewBox="0 0 32 32" role="img" aria-label="{{ who }}">
  <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="16" fill="currentColor" opacity=".22"/>
  <circle cx="16" cy="12.6" r="5" fill="currentColor" opacity=".75"/>
  <path d="M5.6 28.2a10.8 10.8 0 0 1 20.8 0A16 16 0 0 1 5.6 28.2Z" fill="currentColor" opacity=".75"/>
</svg>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
